;;; subject: opendev-terminal-agent-2603 2.2.6 Extended ReAct Execution Loop: the loop that carries out one user query: what runs it and why its reasoning is split from its acting, the phases of one cycle, how a stuck loop is caught and escalated, and how the loop ends
;;; made-from: doc_Base012/docs/Papers-AgentHarness/opendev-terminal-agent/02_agent-core/02_agent-core.lisp / s37 (p-executor-start p-thinking-split-from-acting; s38 .. s44)
;;; members (by role): loop-executor (p-executor-start), loop-purpose (p-thinking-split-from-acting), loop-query-setup (p-query-initialization), phases (p-phase-context-management p-phase-thinking p-phase-action p-phase-dispatch, one copy of the phase sub-frame each), loop-branch (p-phase-decision), loop-repeat-handling (p-stuck-loop-detection), loop-ending-paths and loop-premature-end-guard (p-loop-termination), loop-failures-added-mechanisms (p-failures-that-shaped-the-loop)
;;; children (:frame): phases (each item one copy of opendev.agent-core.react-loop.phase.lisp)
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: the sentence that lists the four approaches considered (p-thinking-split-from-acting/alternatives); the sentence that points to Figure 8 (p-executor-start/figure); the fifth-depth-level history (p-phase-thinking/high-level), the exact thresholds and the two answers a user can give (p-stuck-loop-detection/warn, /allow, /break) and the exact pressure levels (p-phase-context-management/stages) are not blanks of their own: the instructions of loop-repeat-first-response, loop-repeat-escalation and phase ask for them only as "if the harness has such a thing"; the API token count that calibrates the compactor (p-phase-action/calibration) and the way results feed the memory pipeline (p-phase-dispatch/learn) are OpenDev-specific and are left out
(defrule react-loop -> loop-executor loop-purpose loop-query-setup phases loop-branch loop-repeat-handling loop-ending-paths loop-premature-end-guard loop-failures-added-mechanisms)
(defrule loop-executor -> :instruction "問い合わせ 1 件を処理する部品の名前と、それが実装するループの種類を 1 文で書く" :sample "Once a mode is selected, the agent processes each user query through the ReactExecutor, which implements an extended version of the Reason-Act loop [96] (referred to simply as the ReAct loop throughout this paper).")
(defrule loop-purpose -> :background loop-plain-limit :nucleus loop-design-choice)
(defrule loop-plain-limit -> :instruction "素朴な推論と行動の繰り返しが、考える深さを制限する理由を、その原因とともに 1〜2 文で書く。ハーネスが素朴な方式を採るなら、避けられない制限を書く" :sample "Standard ReAct [96] interleaves reasoning and action in the same turn, which limits deliberation. Tool schemas consume context and create pressure to act quickly rather than think deeply.")
(defrule loop-design-choice -> :instruction "このハーネスのループが、考える段階と行動の段階をどう組み合わせるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev combines the latter two: an explicit thinking phase before action, with optional self-critique for complex tasks.")
(defrule loop-query-setup -> :instruction "問い合わせが来たときに、繰り返しの前に整える状態と部品を 1〜2 文で書く。繰り返しをまたいで持つ状態の入れ物があれば、その中身も書く" :sample "When a query arrives, the executor clears any pending injection queue, creates an interrupt token for cancellation support, wraps the conversation history in a ValidatedMessageList (which enforces correct message alternation), and bundles everything into an IterationContext. This context object carries all per-query state: iteration counters, one-shot guard flags (to prevent duplicate signals), and references to shared services such as the tool registry and approval manager.")
(defrule phases -> :instruction "ループの 1 回の繰り返しを構成する段階を、行う順に、1 行に 1 つ段階の名前で挙げる。文脈の管理、考える段階、行動の段階、道具の実行のうち、このハーネスにある段階だけを挙げる" :frame "opendev.agent-core.react-loop.phase.lisp")
(defrule loop-branch -> :instruction "行動の段階の結果が、道具の呼び出しを含むかどうかで処理が分かれることを書く。含まないときの扱いが、失敗の後始末、未完の仕事への催促、終了などに分かれるなら、それも書く" :sample "The executor branches based on whether the action model produced tool calls. If no tool calls are present: when the previous tool failed, the executor classifies the error (permission denied, file not found, syntax error, rate limit, etc.) and injects a targeted recovery nudge (Section 2.3.5); when there are incomplete todos, it nudges the agent to continue; otherwise, a text-only response with no error signals task completion, and the loop terminates.")
(defrule loop-repeat-handling -> :nucleus loop-repeat-detection :elaboration-process-step loop-repeat-first-response :elaboration-process-step loop-repeat-escalation :evaluation-s loop-repeat-assessment)
(defrule loop-repeat-detection -> :instruction "同じ道具の呼び出しの繰り返しを、何を比べ、どの範囲を見て見つけるかを書く。繰り返しを見つける仕組みが無いハーネスでは、段落ごと書かない" :sample "If tool calls are present, the executor first performs doom-loop detection with a two-tier escalation: each tool call is fingerprinted as an MD5 hash of the tool name and its arguments, and fingerprints are tracked in a sliding window of the 20 most recent calls.")
(defrule loop-repeat-first-response -> :instruction "繰り返しを見つけた最初の対処を書く。モデルに何を伝え、その回の道具の実行をどうするか" :sample "If any fingerprint appears 3 or more times, the system injects a [SYSTEM WARNING] message into the conversation (e.g., “ the agent has called read_file with the same arguments 3 times; try a different approach ”) and skips tool execution for that turn.")
(defrule loop-repeat-escalation -> :instruction "最初の対処の後にも繰り返すときの次の対処を書く。人に判断を求めるなら、人の選択肢ごとの動作も書く" :sample "If the same fingerprint recurs after the warning, the system escalates to an approval-based pause via the ApprovalManager, presenting the user with “ Agent is repeating the same action.")
(defrule loop-repeat-assessment -> :instruction "段階を踏む対処が、警告だけの対処より頑丈な理由を書く。従来の粗い歯止めが見逃すものがあれば、それも書く" :sample "This two-tier approach is more robust than warnings alone: LLMs can ignore injected text, but they cannot bypass a genuine execution halt.")
(defrule loop-ending-paths -> :instruction "ループが終わる経路を、種類ごとに書く。明示の完了の合図、道具を呼ばない応答、回復の試行の尽き、繰り返しの回数の上限のうち、このハーネスにあるもの" :sample "The loop ends through one of four paths: the agent explicitly calls a completion tool with a summary and status (success or failure); the agent produces a text response with no tool calls and no error condition (implicit completion); the error-recovery nudge budget is exhausted (three consecutive failed attempts); or the iteration count reaches a configurable safety limit.")
(defrule loop-premature-end-guard -> :instruction "終わりを受け入れる前に確かめることと、終わるときに保存するものを書く。未完の仕事が残る場合の扱いがあれば、それを書く" :sample "If outstanding task items remain when the agent signals completion, the system injects additional nudges to address them before accepting termination to prevent premature completion with incomplete work. In all cases, the final conversation state is persisted to the session store.")
(defrule loop-failures-added-mechanisms -> :instruction "実行の中で観察した失敗が、どの仕組みを足させたか、あるいはどの仕組みの働く範囲を絞らせたかを書く。書き残された経緯が無ければ空にする" :sample "Early experiments applied self-critique on every thinking output; this proved too slow for routine operations, motivating selective activation only at the HIGH thinking level.")
